WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.200
Near a town called Mirzapur, an

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.240
invisible line decides what time

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.040
it is.

4
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.930
For every clock in India.

5
00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:11.609
Indian Standard Time follows the

6
00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:13.449
meridian of eighty two and a

7
00:00:13.449 --> 00:00:15.329
half degrees east.

8
00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:17.829
It runs close to Mirzapur, in

9
00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:19.099
Uttar Pradesh.

10
00:00:19.516 --> 00:00:21.816
The sun covers fifteen degrees

11
00:00:21.816 --> 00:00:23.876
of longitude in an hour.

12
00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:26.296
Eighty two and a half over

13
00:00:26.296 --> 00:00:28.716
fifteen is five and a half.

14
00:00:28.716 --> 00:00:31.636
So Indian time runs five and a

15
00:00:31.636 --> 00:00:34.046
half hours ahead of Greenwich.

16
00:00:34.435 --> 00:00:36.295
But India is wide:

17
00:00:36.295 --> 00:00:38.515
nearly thirty degrees.

18
00:00:38.515 --> 00:00:41.235
At Kibithu, in Arunachal

19
00:00:41.235 --> 00:00:43.615
Pradesh, the sun rises almost

20
00:00:43.615 --> 00:00:45.695
two hours before it does at

21
00:00:45.695 --> 00:00:47.775
Guhar Moti, in Kutch.

22
00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:49.775
The clocks, on the whole,

23
00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:51.065
decline to comment.

24
00:00:51.619 --> 00:00:55.399
It was not always one time.

25
00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:58.679
Calcutta kept its own until

26
00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:01.499
1948, Bombay until 1955.

27
00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:04.639
Indian Standard Time itself

28
00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:06.307
began in 1906.

29
00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:09.265
Today, atomic clocks at the

30
00:01:09.265 --> 00:01:11.645
National Physical Laboratory, in

31
00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:13.435
Delhi, keep it.

32
00:01:13.815 --> 00:01:16.215
India never changes its clocks

33
00:01:16.215 --> 00:01:17.845
for daylight saving.

34
00:01:18.815 --> 00:01:21.255
One line, one district, and a

35
00:01:21.255 --> 00:01:23.055
whole country agrees.

36
00:01:23.055 --> 00:01:25.145
Rare, and on time.

37
00:01:26.384 --> 00:01:26.957
For GS1:

38
00:01:26.957 --> 00:01:29.324
Indian Standard Time uses eighty

39
00:01:29.324 --> 00:01:31.024
two and a half degrees east,

40
00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.024
near Mirzapur.

41
00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:35.224
Five and a half hours ahead of

42
00:01:35.224 --> 00:01:37.204
Greenwich; sunrise differs by

43
00:01:37.204 --> 00:01:39.734
nearly two hours, east to west.

44
00:01:40.504 --> 00:01:42.724
One line on the map.

45
00:01:42.724 --> 00:01:45.214
One time on every wall.
